# quadpack builds and tests with no credentials at all. This file exists so the
# one thing that does need a token has somewhere obvious to live, and so a new
# machine can be set up from the repo alone.
#
# Copy it and fill in what you actually need.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# .env is gitignored. Never commit it. Never paste its contents into an issue,
# a pull request, or a log.
#
# This project shares no credentials with the sibling projects in this
# workspace. Each one gets its own .env at its own root.

# Talking to GitHub from the command line, for pushing and for `gh` in CI.
# A classic personal access token with `repo` scope is enough. A fine grained
# token with read and write on this repository only is better.
#
# It is optional. You only need it for headless git and for the gh CLI, and
# both work from your keyring without it.
# https://github.com/settings/personal-access-tokens
GITHUB_TOKEN=

# Used by the release and benchmark workflows so they do not hardcode an
# account. Not a secret.
GITHUB_OWNER=quefep-bmgo
GITHUB_REPO=quadpack

# Nothing below this line is needed to build, test, or benchmark quadpack.
# quadpack has no dependencies, no services, no database, and no network calls.
#
# If you find yourself adding a token here, check whether the thing you are
# about to authenticate against should just be a build option.